msgctxt "188"
msgid ""
"Thank you for listening. That was an Okinawan folk song called \"The Rose "
"Balsam.\""
msgstr ""

msgctxt "200"
msgid "(He's actually pretty good.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "212"
msgid ""
"A lot of Okinawan folk songs have themes of love⑬like this next tune about "
"a young man pining for a woman. It's called \"The Moon's Beauty.\""
msgstr ""

msgctxt "224"
msgid "If you have some time to spare, why not stay a while and listen?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "236"
msgid "(Not a bad idea.)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "248"
msgid "And now, without further ado... \"The Moon's Beauty.\""
msgstr ""

msgctxt "260"
msgid ""
"Hey! What the hell do you think you're doin'!? Who gave you permission to "
"pollute the airwaves with that wailin'?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "284"
msgid "Eeek!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "296"
msgid "You there, scram! Nothin' left to see here. Get moving!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "308"
msgid "And you! How many times do we gotta tell you to quit that howling?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "320"
msgid ""
"I can perform wherever I want. You don't get to decide where I can and "
"can't sing!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "332"
msgid ""
"We'll see who decides what once I wire your trap shut! We've had it up to "
"here with you and your stupid old-time ditties!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "344"
msgid ""
"Hey! What are you doing? Please, not my grandma's sanshin! You're going to "
"break it!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "356"
msgid ""
"Is it that important to you? Don't worry then, we'll make a real smash hit "
"out of it!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "368"
msgid "(This looks bad...)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "380"
msgid "(......)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "392"
msgid "No! You'll never take my sanshin!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "428"
msgid "Hey! Get back here!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "488"
msgid "You got 100 EXP."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "500"
msgid "You punks are the only things getting smashed today."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "512"
msgid "And who the hell are you? Mind your own damn business, pops!"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "524"
msgid "You wanna stand up for this asswipe, then it's your turn to face the music!"
msgstr ""

